### Layer 3 — Behavioral Graph & Storage

**Purpose:** Persist events, build behavioral entity profiles, represent relationships between entities, and maintain immutable audit records.

**Storage architecture (polyglot):**

| Store | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Event log | ClickHouse | Purpose-built for security log analytics, handling billions of events with sub-second aggregation queries. [Webridge](https://webridge.co/tech-stack/cybersecurity-tech-stack) |
| Behavioral graph | Neo4j Enterprise | Entity relationships, social proximity, event chains |
| Entity profiles & cases | PostgreSQL 16 | Baseline models, risk scores, case records |
| Audit logs | WORM-compliant store | Immutable, tamper-evident, chain-of-custody |
| Hot alert cache | Redis 7 | Real-time deduplication, rate limiting |
| Document search | Elasticsearch 8 | Full-text search on unstructured incident reports |

**Audit log hardening (new in v2.0):**
All system actions, model inferences, alert generations, analyst views, decisions, overrides, and case outcomes are written to a **WORM (Write Once Read Many) compliant log store** with cryptographic hash chaining — providing tamper-evident, blockchain-inspired chain-of-custody records defensible in legal proceedings. Log integrity is verified on a scheduled basis by an independent verification process.

**Behavioral graph model:**

Nodes: Persons (pseudonymized), Locations, Events, Groups, Time Windows.

Edges: `INVOLVED_IN`, `CO-LOCATED_WITH`, `ESCALATION_OF`, `REPORTED_BY`, `LINKED_TO`, `REFERRED_FOR_SUPPORT`, `CASE_RESOLVED_VIA`.

The inclusion of support referral and resolution edges ensures the graph captures positive intervention outcomes, not only risk escalation — enabling longitudinal analysis of what interventions work.

**Retention policy:**
- Active case data: per legal and institutional policy (typically 7 years)
- Non-escalated behavioral events: auto-purged after configurable rolling window (default 90 days), enforced automatically
- Audit logs: immutable, retained per legal minimum (minimum 7 years)
- Right-to-erasure requests: automated workflow with privacy officer confirmation, covering all non-legally-mandated records, with deletion audit log entry

