### Layer 6 — Human Decision Dashboard

**Purpose:** Provide BTAM teams and analysts with a clear, actionable, role-appropriate, and legally defensible interface for reviewing alerts, managing cases, and coordinating interventions.

**Dashboard modules:**

*Alert Center:* Prioritized queue with score, tier, bias flag status, contributing signal summary, and role-appropriate recommended next steps. One-click access to full evidence package.

*Entity Timeline:* Chronological event history per pseudonymized subject. Multi-source event overlay. Annotatable by any BTAM team member with role-stamped case notes. Protective factors and support engagement history displayed alongside risk signals.

*Relationship Map:* Interactive graph visualization of entity relationships and proximity to other flagged or case-active entities. Community detection overlays. Support network visibility (anonymized).

*Case Management:* Full case lifecycle (open → under review → BTAM convened → intervention selected → monitoring → closed). Intervention type tracking (support referral, mediation, accommodation, security escalation, no action with rationale). Outcome logging for longitudinal analysis.

*Multidisciplinary Collaboration:* Secure in-platform messaging between BTAM team members on active cases. Role-based information compartmentalization (mental health clinician notes are not visible to law enforcement liaison without explicit case authorization). Case handoff workflows with structured handoff documentation.

*Intervention Outcomes Tracker:* Longitudinal tracking of intervention appropriateness and subject outcomes (positive trajectory, no change, escalation despite intervention). This data feeds both model refinement and institutional program evaluation.

*Audit Trail:* Every view, action, note, override, and decision immutably logged in the WORM audit store. Reviewer accountability dashboard for supervisors. Exportable for legal and compliance review.

**Access control:**
- Role-based access with need-to-know data segmentation
- Analysts see only cases assigned to their jurisdiction
- Mental health clinician notes stored in compartmented sub-system with separate access controls
- MFA mandatory for all roles
- Session activity logging with anomaly detection on analyst behavior — protecting against insider misuse of the platform itself, with alerts to supervisory tier

