## 6. Bias Detection, Fairness, and Demographic Safeguards

This section is elevated and substantially expanded in v2.0.

### 6.1 Pre-Deployment Fairness Testing

Before any model version is deployed to production:

- Disparate impact analysis across protected characteristic groups (race/ethnicity, disability status, socioeconomic indicators, religion, gender, age)
- Fairness-aware ML library evaluation (e.g., Fairlearn, IBM AI Fairness 360)
- What-if simulations in the Risk Intelligence Engine to test score behavior across demographic variants
- EU AI Act high-risk pre-deployment conformity check — documented and signed by privacy officer

### 6.2 Continuous Bias Monitoring

- **Quarterly bias audits** — full disparate impact analysis across all scoring models and alert tiers
- Alert rate disparity analysis by organizational role, department, and demographic group
- **Automatic suspension threshold:** if disparity ratio exceeds **1.2x** for any protected group at any alert tier, the relevant model component is automatically suspended pending governance board review
- Bias audit results reported to governance board at every quarterly meeting
- Annual third-party independent bias and ethics audit, results published internally to institutional leadership

### 6.3 Bias Flag in Alert Packages

Every alert package includes a bias flag analysis: if SHAP attribution reveals that any feature correlated with a protected characteristic contributed meaningfully to the alert score, this is surfaced to the reviewer with:

- Identity of the contributing feature
- Its SHAP contribution value
- A prominence warning indicating potential proxy bias
- A mandatory reviewer acknowledgment before the case can be escalated

This transforms bias from a background technical concern into a visible, actionable part of the analyst workflow.

### 6.4 Training Data Governance

- Historical institutional data used for model training is audited for over-representation of disciplinary records from specific demographic groups before use
- Known biased historical data (e.g., records from periods with documented discriminatory disciplinary policies) is excluded from training sets
- Diverse and representative training data curation is a standing requirement, reviewed annually

