## 7. Ethical & Legal Governance — Hardened Framework

### 7.1 Absolute Prohibitions (Non-Configurable)

These capabilities cannot be enabled under any circumstances, by any operator, regardless of institutional request:

- Facial recognition or biometric identification from any modality
- Emotion inference or affect recognition (explicitly prohibited under EU AI Act Annex III)
- Profiling based on protected characteristics: race, religion, political belief, sexual orientation, disability, national origin
- Predictive crime probability scoring with no institutional behavioral nexus
- Automated consequences: no system output may trigger any action against an individual without human authorization and documented rationale
- Bulk data sharing with law enforcement without institutional legal review and documented legal basis
- Any inference about group membership from behavioral patterns
- Retrospective profiling of individuals not subject to an active, authorized case

### 7.2 Proportionality Tests

For edge cases and new use scenarios not clearly covered by existing policy, a structured proportionality test is required before processing:

- Is the data processing necessary for the stated safety purpose?
- Is there a less privacy-invasive way to achieve the same objective?
- Are the potential harms to individual privacy proportionate to the safety benefit?
- Has the privacy officer reviewed and approved?

### 7.3 Right to Erasure Automation

Automated right-to-erasure workflows cover all non-legally-mandated records. Requests are:
- Received via a standardized institutional portal
- Reviewed by privacy officer within a defined SLA (default 30 days)
- Executed across all storage layers with cryptographic deletion verification
- Logged in the audit trail (the erasure event itself is retained; the erased data is not)

### 7.4 Data Sovereignty & Deployment Options

Given the sensitivity of the data processed and the evolving regulatory landscape around AI workloads: generative AI and RAG integration on streaming pipelines must be subject to data minimization and PII controls — avoid sending raw PII to any external inference endpoint. [Windows Forum](https://windowsforum.com/threads/real-time-analytics-in-2025-kafka-flink-and-cloud-stacks-for-windows.386017/)

The platform supports:
- **On-premise deployment** (full data sovereignty, recommended for highest-sensitivity institutions)
- **Private cloud / sovereign cloud deployment** (isolated tenant, no cross-tenant data sharing)
- **Hybrid deployment** (analytical compute on-premise, coordination tooling in private cloud)

SaaS deployment with shared infrastructure is not available for this platform. Data residency requirements are contractually enforceable.

### 7.5 Chilling Effect Monitoring

The governance board is responsible for monitoring and reviewing aggregate outcomes for unintended chilling effects — for example, patterns suggesting that awareness of the platform is deterring individuals from using mental health services, anonymous reporting systems, or other legitimate institutional resources. If chilling effects are identified, they are treated as a system failure requiring remediation, not an acceptable operational tradeoff.

