## 12. Design Principles — Final Statement

EW-BRAP v2.0 is built on the recognition that the most dangerous failure mode of this platform is not a missed signal — it is a false accusation, a biased alert, an automated consequence, or a surveillance architecture that erodes the human trust necessary for real safety.

**The platform succeeds when:**
- BTAM teams catch concerning situations early enough to intervene supportively
- Individuals in distress are connected to help before they harm themselves or others
- Analysts trust the alerts enough to act on them without fatigue or cynicism
- Affected communities trust the institution enough to report early and seek help
- Every decision made using platform data can be fully explained, audited, and defended

**The platform fails when:**
- Alerts go unreviewed because false positive rates destroyed confidence
- Certain groups are disproportionately flagged due to training data bias
- Any consequence flows to an individual without human review and documented justification
- The existence of the system deters people from using counseling, reporting tools, or other protective resources
- Any capability listed in the prohibitions section is activated for any reason

These principles are not aspirational. They are architectural requirements. Every technical decision in this blueprint flows from them.

