Appendix D: Risk Scoring Algorithm Details

D.1 Composite Score Formula

```
Risk Score = min(100, max(0,
    (∑(w_s × severity_s) / n_events) × severity_multiplier
    + frequency_factor × log(1 + event_count_30d)
    + escalation_coeff × slope_of_severity_over_60_days
    + cross_source_multiplier × (1 – (1/unique_source_count))
    + contextual_modifier × location_risk_coefficient
    – protective_factor × engagement_score
))
```

· severity_multiplier = 1.0 default, higher for Critical event types
· frequency_factor dampened for high-volume benign events
· engagement_score derived from confirmed counseling attendance, active case management, positive social connections from graph

D.2 Protective Factor Calculation

Protective score = baseline_protective_weight × (sum(protective_evidence_points) / max_points)

Evidence points awarded for:

· Confirmed voluntary counseling session (last 30 days): +20
· Active support program enrollment: +15
· Stable, positive peer connections (graph analysis): +10
· No access control violations in 90 days: +10
· Previous case resolved positively: +15

The protective score can reduce the composite risk by up to 30 points, subject to a floor of the raw severity-weighted score so that protective factors do not mask imminent credible threats.

D.3 Confidence Interval

All risk scores are output as (score, 95%_CI_low, 95%_CI_high) based on Bayesian uncertainty estimation from model ensembles or Monte Carlo dropout. The alert dashboard displays the interval; if the lower bound is below the tier threshold but the point estimate is above, the alert is tagged borderline and analyst discretion is highlighted.

