Appendix E: Bias Audit and Fairness Testing Procedure

Quarterly Audit Process:

1. Extract all alerts generated in the past quarter with risk scores, demographic group tags (from institutional records, pseudonymized and used only for audit).
2. For each protected group G, compute:
   · Alert rate per 1000 individuals
   · False positive rate (from analyst feedback)
   · Conversion rate to cases
3. Calculate disparate impact ratio: (alert_rate_G / alert_rate_reference_group). Reference group is the group with the lowest alert rate.
4. If ratio > 1.2 for any group at any alert tier, automatic suspension of that tier’s ML components (rule-based fallback maintained).
5. Governance board reviews and either lifts suspension with documented justification or mandates model retraining.

Pre-Deployment Fairness Test:

· Run backtesting on historical data (with known outcomes) across all demographic groups.
· Measure equal opportunity difference, average odds difference, and demographic parity.
· All models must meet the 1.2 ratio threshold before production deployment.

Bias Flag in Alerts (Technical)

· SHAP values computed for each feature contributing to risk score.
· If any feature tagged in the feature registry as bias_proxy (e.g., zip code, previous discipline count in a skewed dataset) contributes more than 10% of the total positive SHAP value, the alert is flagged with that feature’s name and contribution.
· Feature registry maintained by privacy officer; reviewed quarterly.

