Appendix F: Data Retention, Deletion, and Right to Erasure

Retention Policy (Automated Enforcement):

Data Category Retention Period Trigger
Active case files 7 years from case closure Institution policy
Non-escalated behavioral events 90 days from event time Rolling purge job (daily)
Audit logs (WORM) Minimum 7 years Legal hold
Analytics training data (anonymized) 10 years IRB-approved research
Pseudonymized graph edges Same as source event retention Tied to event

Right to Erasure Workflow:

1. Request received via institutional portal → tagged with entity pseudonym.
2. Privacy officer reviews within 5 business days; confirms legal basis.
3. Automated job:
   · Deletes all non-escalated event records for that entity (any data not tied to an active or closed case).
   · For cases, marks all PII-related fields for deletion upon case closure if not legally required.
   · Cascades deletion across ClickHouse, Elasticsearch, PostgreSQL, and graph database.
4. Cryptographic verification of deletion using hash comparison of data blocks.
5. Deletion event logged in WORM audit store: erasure_request_id, entity_pseudonym, scope, timestamp, verifier_signature.

Legal Hold Override: If a case is under active legal hold, erasure is partially deferred; entity data is masked but retained until hold release, tracked by the compliance module.

