Appendix I: Privacy Impact Assessment (PIA) Template

Required Sections:

1. Data Source Description – What data, from where, volume, frequency.
2. Purpose and Legal Basis – Specific safety objective, legal authority (e.g., institutional policy, GDPR Art.6(1)(f)).
3. Data Minimization – How PII will be removed or pseudonymized at collection; fields that will not be retained.
4. Risk to Individuals – Likelihood and severity of privacy harm (identifiability, re‑identification, chilling effects).
5. Mitigations – Pseudonymization, access controls, retention limits, audit logging.
6. Proportionality Assessment – Alternative less intrusive means considered and why rejected; net benefit to safety outweighing privacy intrusion.
7. Stakeholder Consultation – BTAM team, privacy officer, legal, employee/student representatives.
8. Sign-off – Privacy Officer, Legal Counsel, Governance Board Chair.

